          "derivation": "MP warrag 'lamb, ram; Aries' (PHD), written wlk', is a direct continuation of *varnaka-, with -rn- > -rr-. This part is confirmed. The bird names vāra-γna-/vārəγan- and vārən-jan- (Nourai's 'vâren-žar', Pokorny's 'varan-jar-') are Avestan, not Pahlavi. They occur in Yašt 14.19 and 14.35 as the bird form of Vərəθraγna. Humbach reads them as *vara-γna- 'lamb-slayer' (vara- 'lamb' + -γna- 'striking', PIE *gʷʰen-). Pokorny accepts this, but Bartholomae left the meaning open ('Eig. Bed.?'), so the reading is plausible but not settled. MP warāγ means 'crow' (PHD). Calling it 'lamb killer' depends on the same Humbach analysis.",
